<title>SPAIN: Spanish 1997 budget - Economic forecasts detailed.</title>
<headline>Spanish 1997 budget - Economic forecasts detailed.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish government based its budget on the following economic assumptions: (figures are percentage changes unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>					  1996     1997</p>
<p> Nominal GDP			   6.4	6.0</p>
<p> Real GDP				2.3	3.0</p>
<p> Private consumption		 2.1	2.7</p>
<p> Public consumption		  0.3     -0.3</p>
<p> Gross capital formation	   4.4	5.9</p>
<p>     -construction		   0.5	3.2</p>
<p>     -capital goods		  7.7     12.0</p>
<p>     -stock change		   0.3	0.1</p>
<p> Total internal demand	     2.3	3.2</p>
<p> Exports				 7.5	8.5</p>
<p> Imports				 7.3	8.7</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
